language Essence 1.3
$ Compare sums of set elements and signed Boolean terms.
$ Compare two sums directly, including negative coefficients and inequalities.
find a,b,c,d,e : set (size 1) of int(1..3)
find p,q,r,s : bool
such that
    (sum i in a . i) = (sum i in b . i),
    (sum i in a . i*i) = (sum i in b . i*i),
    (sum i in a . i) >= (sum i in c . i),
    (sum i in b . i) <= (sum i in c . i),
    (sum i in d . i) = (sum i in e . 2*i),
    sum([-2*toInt(p),3*toInt(q)]) = sum([-2*toInt(r),3*toInt(s)]),
    sum([-2*toInt(p),3*toInt(q)]) != sum([-2*toInt(r),3*toInt(s),1]),
    sum([-2*toInt(p),3*toInt(q)]) < sum([-2*toInt(r),3*toInt(s),1]),
    sum([-2*toInt(p),3*toInt(q),1]) > sum([-2*toInt(r),3*toInt(s)])
